@baseUrl = http://localhost:5080
# Replace these with the IDs returned by the two POST requests below.
@sourceId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000
@destinationId = 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000

### Create Alice (copy the returned id into sourceId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerName": "Alice",
  "initialBalance": 500
}

### Create Bob (copy the returned id into destinationId)
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/accounts
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "ownerName": "Bob",
  "initialBalance": 50
}

### Transfer 100
POST {{baseUrl}}/api/transfers
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sourceAccountId": "{{sourceId}}",
  "destinationAccountId": "{{destinationId}}",
  "amount": 100
}

### Alice should now have 400
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accounts/{{sourceId}}

### Bob should now have 150
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/accounts/{{destinationId}}

### History
GET {{baseUrl}}/api/transfers
